cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below (and cite the original paper too)."
title: "A proof of Conjecture A.1 of Liu-Wu-Zhang-Zhou, with sharpness analysis and a partial Lean formalisation"
abstract: >-
  Complete proof of Conjecture A.1 from the Appendix A of Liu-Wu-Zhang-Zhou,
  Comm. Math. Phys. 375 (2020) 785-832: for central Z = [X,Y] = XY - YX and
  X^{p+1}v = Y^{q+1}v = 0 one has (X+Y)^{2p+2q+1}v = 0, for all p, q >= 0.
  The repository also contains a technical note on the methods used, a rigorous
  sharpness analysis (sharp for p = 0 or q = 0; verified for p,q <= 6;
  open in general), exact rational arithmetic verification scripts, and a
  partial (uncompiled) Lean 4 formalisation with a detailed gap report.
